        "original_id": "288e5106-3278-5868-b093-40b739e70cbb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Musselman, Bill Musselman, Chuck Daly, Doc Rivers, Lon Kruger, Yanni Hufnagel, Rudy D'Amico\n- Organizations: Continental Basketball Association, Minnesota Timberwolves, Orlando Magic, Atlanta Hawks, Detroit Pistons, United States men's Olympic basketball team, Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team\n- Roles: head coach, assistant coach, scout\n\nFacts:\n- Chuck Daly was an American basketball head coach who was born on July 20, 1930, and died on May 9, 2009.\n- Chuck Daly led the Detroit Pistons to consecutive NBA championships in 1989 and 1990.\n- Chuck Daly led the 1992 United States men's Olympic basketball team, known as the Dream Team, to the gold medal at the 1992 Summer Olympics.\n- Eric Musselman is the son of former NBA head coach Bill Musselman.\n- Eric Musselman was a head coach in the Continental Basketball Association before becoming an assistant coach with the Minnesota Timberwolves, Orlando Magic, and Atlanta Hawks.\n- Eric Musselman served under Chuck Daly and Doc Rivers with the Orlando Magic and under Lon Kruger with the Atlanta Hawks.\n- Yanni Hufnagel last served as an assistant coach of the Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team under Eric Musselman.\n- Rudy D'Amico scouts for the Orlando Magic.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
